# Builds `filingagent-qwen3` — qwen3:8b with a context window that fits a
# 6GB consumer GPU. Run `make model` once; docker-compose points LLM_MODEL here.
#
# Why this is a checked-in file rather than a README note:
#
# Ollama sizes its KV cache from the model's FULL context window unless told
# otherwise. For qwen3:8b that default is 40960 tokens, which turns a 5.2GB
# model into an 11GB reservation. On a 6GB card the result is not "slower" —
# it is a hard failure:
#
#     HTTP 500: model requires more system memory (5.6 GiB)
#               than is available (5.3 GiB)
#
# because the overflow spills to host RAM a normal desktop session has already
# spent. Measured on an RTX 3050 6GB / 15.4GB RAM laptop:
#
#     default 40960  ->  11.0GB reservation, 54% CPU, 500 error under load
#     capped  12288  ->   7.2GB reservation, 26% CPU, 13.5s per tool turn
#
# 12288 is sized from the real workload, not guessed. A retrieval prompt is
# ~2,010 tokens (5 chunks at baseline._TOP_K, measured against the built
# index), and the worst realistic case is an agent spending all 5 turns on
# search_filings: ~11,000 tokens including the ~1,500-token tool schemas.
# 12288 clears that. 8192 would silently truncate it, which is worse than
# failing loudly — the arm still answers, just from a context with the
# evidence cut off, and it scores as a reasoning failure.
#
# Raise it if you have more VRAM. Every increase buys headroom and costs GPU
# residency, and residency is what makes this fast.

FROM qwen3:8b

PARAMETER num_ctx 12288
